  "id": "day-blindness",
  "term": "day blindness",
  "definition": "Day blindness is a symptom, not a separate disorder, in which a person sees poorly in strong light and may see better in dim light or at night. A brief, normal form can happen when moving suddenly from darkness into bright light; the opposite condition is night blindness.",
